  "body": "<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\nAdds a small note clarifying 103 Early Hints recommendation to only use with HTTP/2 or later unless it is known the implementation supports this, as noted in the [IETF RFC](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8297#section-3), and explains why examples are still in HTTP/1.1-style.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Already implemented in Chrome (103 - nice coincidence!) and Safari (16.6 and 17). WIP for Firefox.\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * Clarification. Tests already written at https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/loading/early-hints\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: Only implemented for HTTP/2\n   * Gecko: Does [support over HTTP/1](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1813035#c6) but still behind a flag.\n   * WebKit: [Only implement for HTTP/2](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/10836)\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): …\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): …\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n   Clarification PR raised here: https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/28214\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9563/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 1, 2023, 4:52 AM UTC (c9b6e39)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9563/b729c06...c9b6e39/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 1, 2023, 4:52 AM UTC (c9b6e39)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9563/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 1, 2023, 4:52 AM UTC (c9b6e39)\">/semantics.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9563/b729c06...c9b6e39/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 1, 2023, 4:52 AM UTC (c9b6e39)\">diff</a> )",
